WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.370 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.210 --> 01:37.890
[Episode 33]

4
01:48.900 --> 01:53.150
[Mianning Yi Village, Liangshan, Sichuan]

5
02:09.680 --> 02:12.110
[Xiaoyedan, Head of the Guoji branch of the Yi people]

6
02:11.460 --> 02:12.300
Xiaoyedan.

7
02:13.910 --> 02:14.840
Xiaoyedan,

8
02:15.630 --> 02:17.400
why do you just sit here all the time?

9
02:17.400 --> 02:20.560
The Han army has already pushed into our Yi territory.

10
02:20.650 --> 02:22.910
You need to think about what we should do.

11
02:23.000 --> 02:24.590
I heard that

12
02:25.079 --> 02:27.470
the Luohong and Luowu clans

13
02:27.840 --> 02:29.310
have already taken to the woods,

14
02:29.310 --> 02:30.710
preparing for battle.

15
02:30.730 --> 02:33.760
Our Guoji clan can't just sit back and watch.

16
02:34.020 --> 02:35.900
We need to gather our men right now

17
02:36.390 --> 02:37.670
and get ready to fight.

18
02:43.900 --> 02:44.810
Uncle,

19
02:45.010 --> 02:46.410
you can read Han writing.

20
02:46.570 --> 02:49.130
Take a look at this notice they posted.

21
02:54.360 --> 02:58.120
"The Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

22
02:58.240 --> 03:01.360
fights for the poor.

23
03:01.490 --> 03:02.890
They treat their Yi brothers

24
03:02.890 --> 03:05.170
as their own kin,

25
03:05.320 --> 03:07.890
even closer than their own flesh and blood."

26
03:09.560 --> 03:10.750
You believe that?

27
03:13.840 --> 03:14.680
Uncle,

28
03:14.870 --> 03:16.060
keep reading.

29
03:19.079 --> 03:22.079
"The Red Army fights for the interests of the working masses,

30
03:22.079 --> 03:22.960
paving the way to a bright future.

31
03:22.960 --> 03:26.240
No obstacle can hold us back.

32
03:26.310 --> 03:28.750
Now that we've reached western Sichuan,

33
03:28.770 --> 03:32.900
we won't try to change any of the Yi people's customs.

34
03:33.350 --> 03:36.230
We won't oppress them.

35
03:36.250 --> 03:38.880
Nor will we take their grain for nothing.

36
03:38.910 --> 03:43.720
We act with mutual respect and follow the rules.

37
03:48.030 --> 03:50.120
All Yi people living here

38
03:50.520 --> 03:52.190
should strive to

39
03:52.400 --> 03:56.060
establish their own people's government and manage themselves,

40
03:56.140 --> 04:00.530
achieving equality for all, free from oppression."

41
04:02.200 --> 04:03.890
This notice

42
04:04.360 --> 04:06.020
is different from the others.

43
04:06.760 --> 04:08.700
Every word of it speaks straight to my heart.

44
04:08.700 --> 04:09.700
Xiaoyedan,

45
04:10.850 --> 04:12.710
you're not a three-year-old kid.

46
04:12.730 --> 04:15.200
You're our respected chief.

47
04:15.430 --> 04:17.660
For all these years,

48
04:17.680 --> 04:23.200
haven't we seen enough of these people saying one thing and doing another?

49
04:23.270 --> 04:27.750
Haven't they committed enough atrocities?

50
04:27.860 --> 04:30.650
Are these Red Army soldiers really any different?

51
04:30.650 --> 04:31.290
Uncle,

52
04:31.320 --> 04:34.440
you know a horse by riding it, and an ox by plowing with it.

53
04:34.440 --> 04:36.840
I sent Shama'erge over to check things out.

54
04:36.890 --> 04:38.600
Let's wait for him to get back and report.

55
04:38.600 --> 04:39.880
Xiaoyedan!

56
04:40.240 --> 04:41.630
Chief Xiaoyedan!

57
04:41.820 --> 04:43.090
Chief Xiaoyedan!

58
04:45.810 --> 04:46.980
Chief Xiaoyedan!

59
04:49.430 --> 04:50.430
Shama'erge,

60
04:51.010 --> 04:52.190
what's the situation?

61
04:52.190 --> 04:55.870
Those people were so stunned they couldn't even speak.

62
04:56.050 --> 04:57.630
They just stood there staring with their mouths wide open.

63
04:57.630 --> 05:00.290
They didn't even fight back when we kicked them.

64
05:00.570 --> 05:01.400
Let me see.

65
05:03.630 --> 05:04.980
How many of them are there?

66
05:04.980 --> 05:06.240
I saw about thirty men.

67
05:06.510 --> 05:08.720
And in Mianning

68
05:08.870 --> 05:12.470
and Mount Xiaoxiangling, a huge number of troops are stationed.

69
05:12.720 --> 05:15.000
I heard they're all gathering here,

70
05:15.000 --> 05:17.130
passing right through our territory.

71
05:22.220 --> 05:26.030
These soldiers didn't even want their guns anymore.

72
05:26.160 --> 05:27.820
I can't wrap my head around it.

73
05:28.500 --> 05:32.230
I don't understand it either.

74
05:32.600 --> 05:34.390
And we aren't the only ones who took their guns.

75
05:34.390 --> 05:36.120
The Luohong clan took some too.

76
05:36.159 --> 05:38.159
They didn't dare fight back either.

77
06:08.200 --> 06:09.120
Shama'erge,

78
06:09.360 --> 06:10.970
I drew your knife.

79
06:11.160 --> 06:12.760
Why didn't you say anything?

80
06:13.870 --> 06:17.920
How could I? You're my chief.

81
06:17.920 --> 06:20.950
We grew up together, as close as brothers.

82
06:24.070 --> 06:24.830
Uncle,

83
06:25.020 --> 06:28.340
the way I see it, they're sincere.

84
06:28.640 --> 06:31.720
The Han and the Yi really are brothers.

85
06:31.900 --> 06:34.820
Only true brothers would act like this.

86
06:35.040 --> 06:35.950
Xiaoyedan.

87
06:36.720 --> 06:37.450
Shama'erge,

88
06:38.120 --> 06:40.000
take me to see their commander.

89
06:40.040 --> 06:40.570
Let's go.

90
06:41.370 --> 06:42.330
Wait a minute!

91
06:45.990 --> 06:46.870
Xiaoyedan,

92
06:47.720 --> 06:48.980
what's wrong with you?

93
06:49.190 --> 06:51.720
They put up all these notices for us to see

94
06:51.950 --> 06:53.740
and let us have a few guns,

95
06:53.950 --> 06:56.350
and you aren't even thinking this through?

96
06:57.040 --> 06:58.000
I heard

97
06:58.320 --> 07:00.410
Mianning has already been taken by them,

98
07:00.410 --> 07:02.240
and a lot of people were killed.

99
07:02.410 --> 07:05.410
My poor son,

100
07:05.750 --> 07:09.420
Amu... I don't even know if he's dead or alive.

101
07:12.010 --> 07:15.010
Xiaoyedan, I agree.

102
07:15.830 --> 07:17.350
I agree too.

103
07:17.810 --> 07:19.290
You shouldn't go.

104
07:20.440 --> 07:21.240
Don't go.

105
07:22.540 --> 07:23.290
Uncle,

106
07:24.190 --> 07:25.760
Shama'erge already told us.

107
07:25.760 --> 07:27.220
These men are good people.

108
07:27.720 --> 07:29.310
Are we really going to war with good men

109
07:29.310 --> 07:31.310
just to prove our bravery and honor?

110
07:31.530 --> 07:33.440
We took their guns,

111
07:33.750 --> 07:35.550
and they didn't even fight back.

112
07:35.630 --> 07:36.480
The way I see it,

113
07:36.480 --> 07:39.070
they are honorable, true men.

114
07:40.510 --> 07:41.240
Yedan!

115
07:41.670 --> 07:43.380
What is wrong with you?

116
07:44.190 --> 07:46.360
They put up a few posters for us,

117
07:46.720 --> 07:48.340
gave us some guns,

118
07:48.740 --> 07:50.870
and you think that makes them true men?

119
07:51.840 --> 07:53.080
Father!

120
07:53.520 --> 07:54.810
Father!

121
07:56.110 --> 07:56.960
Father!

122
07:57.310 --> 07:58.120
Amu!

123
07:58.140 --> 07:58.990
Father!

124
07:59.870 --> 08:00.750
Amu!

125
08:01.230 --> 08:03.040
Amu is back!

126
08:03.060 --> 08:04.940
Am I seeing this right?

127
08:05.600 --> 08:06.360
It's me.

128
08:07.210 --> 08:08.010
I'm alive.

129
08:08.040 --> 08:09.930
You're really alive!

130
08:11.990 --> 08:13.790
I thought you were killed

131
08:13.820 --> 08:15.630
by those devilish soldiers.

132
08:16.650 --> 08:17.500
Amu,

133
08:17.870 --> 08:19.060
how did you get back?

134
08:20.960 --> 08:22.080
Chief Yedan,

135
08:23.950 --> 08:26.280
the Red Army has reached Mianning County.

136
08:26.480 --> 08:27.980
They chased off that scum of a magistrate

137
08:27.980 --> 08:29.230
and scared away all his men!

138
08:29.230 --> 08:31.080
The Red Army let me go.

139
08:31.310 --> 08:32.240
Did you see the Red Army?

140
08:32.240 --> 08:32.750
I did.

141
08:32.960 --> 08:33.820
The Red Army...

142
08:34.070 --> 08:35.710
their top commander...

143
08:36.030 --> 08:37.030
gave me food

144
08:37.049 --> 08:38.049
and called me...

145
08:38.789 --> 08:39.600
called me...

146
08:40.840 --> 08:42.030
brother.

147
08:42.360 --> 08:43.120
I...

148
08:43.330 --> 08:48.610
Everyone wearing a red star called me brother.

149
08:57.120 --> 08:58.420
Look, is it this red star?

150
08:58.420 --> 09:00.190
Yes, that's the one!

151
09:01.050 --> 09:03.620
Chief Yedan, how do you have that?

152
09:04.790 --> 09:05.600
Uncle,

153
09:06.890 --> 09:08.370
do you believe it now?

154
09:15.400 --> 09:16.440
I believe it.

155
09:16.580 --> 09:18.780
This is an army of good men. I believe it.

156
09:20.720 --> 09:22.780
Now I'm going to meet their commander.

157
09:22.780 --> 09:24.270
Any objections?

158
09:24.670 --> 09:25.750
Shama'erge!

159
09:25.850 --> 09:27.040
Let's go. Let's go.

160
09:30.240 --> 09:34.640
[Yihai Lake, Mianning, Liangshan, Sichuan]

161
09:32.270 --> 09:34.790
On May 22, 1935,

162
09:34.790 --> 09:36.510
Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Red Army

163
09:36.510 --> 09:39.600
and Commander of the Vanguard Detachment,

164
09:39.750 --> 09:43.240
arranged to meet with Xiaoyedan,

165
09:41.880 --> 09:45.030
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Red Army and concurrently Commander of the Military Commission Column]

166
09:43.260 --> 09:46.320
Head of the Guoji branch of the Yi people, by Yihai Lake.

167
09:46.320 --> 09:49.150
Liu Bocheng detailed to Xiaoyedan

168
09:49.170 --> 09:51.640
the CPC and Red Army's

169
09:51.670 --> 09:53.340
policies advocating equality between Yi and Han peoples

170
09:53.340 --> 09:55.570
and jointly resisting oppression.

171
09:56.130 --> 09:58.440
Deeply moved, Xiaoyedan

172
09:58.570 --> 10:00.310
[Xiao Hua, Director of the Organization Department, Political Department of the 1st Red Army Corps]

173
09:58.760 --> 10:02.400
proposed becoming sworn brothers with Liu Bocheng.

174
10:03.650 --> 10:05.080
By the waters of Yihai,

175
10:05.220 --> 10:06.770
following Yi customs,

176
10:07.080 --> 10:09.920
they drank lake water as wine to seal their brotherhood.

177
10:09.920 --> 10:11.010
This forged the legendary

178
10:11.010 --> 10:13.130
Yihai Alliance of the Long March.

179
10:13.800 --> 10:14.530
Afterwards,

180
10:14.790 --> 10:18.120
Liu Bocheng presented Xiaoyedan, on behalf of the Red Army,

181
10:18.140 --> 10:19.600
with the banner of the Guoji Detachment

182
10:19.600 --> 10:21.340
of the Chinese Yi People's Red Army,

183
10:21.340 --> 10:23.340
as well as some weapons and equipment.

184
10:21.530 --> 10:28.920
[Guoji Detachment of the Chinese Yi People's Red Army]

185
10:26.690 --> 10:27.540
Xiaoyedan,

186
10:27.830 --> 10:29.760
do you know the biggest difference

187
10:29.960 --> 10:31.390
between our Red Army

188
10:31.670 --> 10:33.310
and the Kuomintang forces?

189
10:34.220 --> 10:35.340
What is it?

190
10:36.460 --> 10:38.320
The Kuomintang forces do nothing

191
10:38.400 --> 10:41.040
but deceive and oppress

192
10:41.060 --> 10:43.330
us laboring masses.

193
10:43.640 --> 10:44.830
Yes, you're right.

194
10:45.080 --> 10:46.390
But our Red Army

195
10:46.790 --> 10:48.520
is here to liberate the masses,

196
10:48.920 --> 10:52.670
and free the suffering poor everywhere.

197
10:54.370 --> 10:55.920
Do you know what our Red Army

198
10:56.130 --> 10:57.520
and our Yi brothers

199
10:58.070 --> 11:00.620
have most in common?

200
11:01.390 --> 11:02.200
First of all,

201
11:02.430 --> 11:04.040
we are all equals.

202
11:04.500 --> 11:06.860
No one is above or below anyone else.

203
11:07.750 --> 11:08.550
Besides,

204
11:08.980 --> 11:13.150
the Yi people are all persecuted poor folks,

205
11:13.550 --> 11:15.550
and the vast majority of our Red Army

206
11:15.750 --> 11:17.600
also come from poor backgrounds.

207
11:17.600 --> 11:18.930
Take me for example.

208
11:20.020 --> 11:22.620
I'm from Kai County, Sichuan.

209
11:24.590 --> 11:25.950
When I was just a boy,

210
11:26.180 --> 11:28.140
my father passed away.

211
11:29.080 --> 11:31.670
My mother raised us

212
11:32.320 --> 11:34.320
entirely on her own.

213
11:34.920 --> 11:36.440
Life was very hard.

214
11:37.240 --> 11:39.000
You saw it yourself today

215
11:39.270 --> 11:40.910
that young comrade Xiao Hua

216
11:41.180 --> 11:42.750
is a bricklayer's son.

217
11:44.100 --> 11:45.170
And those other

218
11:45.200 --> 11:46.970
young soldiers

219
11:47.240 --> 11:50.070
are all children of poor families.

220
11:50.550 --> 11:51.840
This shows

221
11:52.000 --> 11:53.070
that our Red Army

222
11:53.240 --> 11:56.880
is an army of poor people united

223
11:57.090 --> 12:00.370
to fight the Kuomintang troops

224
12:00.400 --> 12:01.430
who oppress us.

225
12:02.880 --> 12:04.000
So tell me,

226
12:04.510 --> 12:07.790
are the Red Army and the Yi people

227
12:07.910 --> 12:09.030
one family?

228
12:09.160 --> 12:10.130
We are.

229
12:10.750 --> 12:12.210
You're absolutely right.

230
12:12.330 --> 12:14.850
We'll be heading out tomorrow.

231
12:16.260 --> 12:17.470
You must stay here

232
12:18.200 --> 12:20.670
and keep up the fight.

233
12:21.580 --> 12:22.580
Bocheng,

234
12:23.150 --> 12:25.630
why don't you stay a couple more days?

235
12:25.730 --> 12:26.910
Give the troops a rest.

236
12:26.910 --> 12:28.200
There's no time.

237
12:29.440 --> 12:31.530
When we achieve victory,

238
12:32.680 --> 12:35.840
I'll bring the comrades back.

239
12:35.950 --> 12:36.480
Alright.

240
12:36.500 --> 12:38.230
Then we'll get together again,

241
12:38.560 --> 12:40.890
eat meat, drink, and dance.

242
12:40.910 --> 12:41.600
Good.

243
12:41.960 --> 12:43.470
Whatever you say, Bocheng.

244
12:43.470 --> 12:44.440
Have a seat.

245
12:45.580 --> 12:46.350
Sit.

246
12:52.640 --> 12:53.680
Bocheng,

247
12:54.480 --> 12:55.750
I never imagined

248
12:55.960 --> 12:57.630
you'd trust me so much.

249
12:58.180 --> 12:59.610
We're sworn brothers.

250
12:59.890 --> 13:01.090
Of course I trust you.

251
13:02.670 --> 13:03.910
This flag

252
13:04.430 --> 13:07.160
doesn't just bear witness to our friendship

253
13:07.550 --> 13:10.670
and the brotherhood between the Yi and Han peoples.

254
13:12.210 --> 13:15.490
It also means that from now on,

255
13:16.320 --> 13:18.960
you and I

256
13:19.390 --> 13:23.630
are revolutionary comrades with a shared ideal.

257
13:23.910 --> 13:25.390
Revolutionary comrades!

258
13:25.410 --> 13:28.290
Yes, revolutionary comrades.

259
13:28.910 --> 13:29.630
Bocheng,

260
13:29.910 --> 13:33.630
this red flag is the token of our support for the Red Army.

261
13:34.810 --> 13:36.470
With Yihai Lake as my witness,

262
13:36.720 --> 13:37.840
I swear

263
13:38.140 --> 13:39.230
that at all times,

264
13:39.750 --> 13:41.750
I will defend this flag with my life.

265
13:41.940 --> 13:43.140
As long as I'm around,

266
13:43.140 --> 13:45.690
the flag of the Red Army Yi Detachment

267
13:46.400 --> 13:47.800
will never fall.

268
13:51.120 --> 13:52.000
Xiaoyedan,

269
13:53.040 --> 13:55.890
I also promise you

270
13:56.720 --> 13:57.650
that our Red Army

271
13:57.910 --> 14:00.390
will never forget this detachment.

272
14:01.240 --> 14:02.270
And I

273
14:02.390 --> 14:05.200
will never forget my good brother,

274
14:05.720 --> 14:06.840
Xiaoyedan.

275
14:13.930 --> 14:14.770
Bocheng,

276
14:15.570 --> 14:17.170
you're leaving tomorrow.

277
14:18.040 --> 14:20.130
Let me sing you a Yi song

278
14:21.440 --> 14:22.550
to see you off.

279
14:23.870 --> 14:24.550
Okay.

280
14:32.330 --> 14:35.810
♪ Keep company with auspicious friends ♪

281
14:35.840 --> 14:38.630
Starting May 23, 1935,

282
14:39.120 --> 14:40.840
the Red Army troops, guided by Xiaoyedan

283
14:40.840 --> 14:44.360
and his people, safely crossed the Yi region

284
14:44.380 --> 14:46.710
and advanced toward the Dadu River.

285
14:47.150 --> 14:47.910
Afterward,

286
14:48.030 --> 14:50.700
Xiaoyedan followed Liu Bocheng's instructions,

287
14:50.700 --> 14:53.180
actively united other Yi clans,

288
14:53.460 --> 14:56.590
and persisted in the revolutionary fight in Liangshan.

289
14:57.100 --> 14:59.650
On June 18, 1942,

290
15:00.010 --> 15:02.130
Xiaoyedan, who was only 48,

291
15:02.160 --> 15:03.870
was attacked by tribal armed forces

292
15:03.870 --> 15:05.300
bought off by the Kuomintang army

293
15:05.300 --> 15:06.810
and died a heroic death.

294
15:07.160 --> 15:09.760
To protect the banner of the Yi Detachment,

295
15:10.040 --> 15:12.370
Xiaoyedan's wife, Luowu Wujimo,

296
15:12.590 --> 15:14.360
sewed it into

297
15:14.390 --> 15:16.950
the lining of her pleated skirt.

298
15:17.680 --> 15:20.400
In 1950, when Mianning was liberated,

299
15:20.860 --> 15:23.930
Luowu Wujimo presented the flag to the government.

300
15:24.180 --> 15:26.350
The flag is now preserved in

301
15:26.430 --> 15:29.630
the Military Museum of the Chinese People's Revolution.

302
15:32.140 --> 15:33.630
Take your time.

303
15:35.010 --> 15:37.330
Walk slowly. Be careful.

304
15:38.850 --> 15:39.760
Bocheng!

305
15:41.500 --> 15:43.070
You must come back.

306
15:43.610 --> 15:45.010
I'll wait for you here.

307
15:46.400 --> 15:47.440
Xiaoyedan,

308
15:48.010 --> 15:49.370
please believe us.

309
15:51.080 --> 15:52.880
We will definitely come back.

310
15:53.790 --> 15:55.960
All right, all right.

311
15:56.120 --> 15:57.600
You must come back.

312
15:58.200 --> 15:59.390
I'll be waiting for you.

313
15:59.390 --> 16:00.200
Okay.

314
16:06.770 --> 16:11.680
[Fan Shaozeng's Residence, Chongqing]

315
16:08.480 --> 16:15.050
♪ Since we became sworn brothers at Caoqiao ♪

316
16:15.520 --> 16:20.090
♪ We've shared a desk for three springs ♪

317
16:22.200 --> 16:26.630
♪ I never knew you were a girl in disguise ♪

318
16:27.440 --> 16:33.080
♪ How could I have been so blind ♪

319
16:36.440 --> 16:37.130
Generalissimo,

320
16:37.130 --> 16:38.490
it rains a lot in Chongqing this time of year.

321
16:38.490 --> 16:39.610
Please take care not to catch a cold.

322
16:39.610 --> 16:40.610
I'll be fine.

323
16:41.150 --> 16:42.110
Did you know?

324
16:42.420 --> 16:43.750
Seventy-two years ago,

325
16:43.870 --> 16:45.600
Shi Dakai stood right here

326
16:45.600 --> 16:47.600
by the Dadu River after a heavy rain

327
16:47.870 --> 16:50.330
and lamented, "A great river blocks my path.

328
16:50.390 --> 16:52.580
How can I cross these rushing waters?"

329
16:52.890 --> 16:54.210
His entire army was wiped out.

330
16:54.210 --> 16:55.100
Generalissimo,

331
16:55.100 --> 16:58.030
this time the Zhu-Mao communist forces are surely doomed.

332
16:58.030 --> 16:58.560
Exactly.

333
16:58.660 --> 17:01.060
I'm hoping this early summer rain

334
17:01.220 --> 17:03.770
not only pours down on Chongqing,

335
17:03.800 --> 17:06.520
but also pounds the Dadu River.

336
17:06.760 --> 17:08.430
I just want to know right now

337
17:08.450 --> 17:11.490
what Mao Zedong is thinking.

338
17:15.380 --> 17:18.339
Are you two hungry?

339
17:19.720 --> 17:20.770
I'm all right.

340
17:21.089 --> 17:23.400
You know I don't eat spicy food,

341
17:23.700 --> 17:26.869
but I can treat you to some meat,

342
17:27.190 --> 17:28.670
noodles,

343
17:28.900 --> 17:30.380
and wontons.

344
17:30.430 --> 17:31.520
The Generalissimo is treating us!

345
17:31.520 --> 17:32.850
Sounds great!

346
17:33.030 --> 17:34.440
All right, let's go.

347
17:34.490 --> 17:35.600
Generalissimo.

348
17:39.670 --> 17:44.070
[Yuexi County, Sichuan]

349
18:09.250 --> 18:11.290
A great river blocks my path.

350
18:11.930 --> 18:13.990
How can I cross these rushing waters?

351
18:14.760 --> 18:15.960
I really want to know,

352
18:16.410 --> 18:17.210
back then,

353
18:18.290 --> 18:20.490
what kind of look was in Shi Dakai's eyes

354
18:20.630 --> 18:22.090
when he was defeated here.

355
18:23.050 --> 18:23.850
Chairman,

356
18:23.980 --> 18:25.610
what does this tablet say?

357
18:26.020 --> 18:27.020
Zidadi.

358
18:28.020 --> 18:29.370
Where is Zidadi?

359
18:29.590 --> 18:32.550
It's where the Wing King, Shi Dakai, was defeated.

360
18:33.470 --> 18:35.270
It's what we now call Anshunchang.

361
18:35.270 --> 18:35.980
Chairman,

362
18:36.300 --> 18:38.330
aren't we heading to Anshunchang too?

363
18:38.330 --> 18:39.170
We are.

364
18:39.460 --> 18:40.420
In 1863,

365
18:40.880 --> 18:42.090
Shi Dakai

366
18:42.480 --> 18:43.750
arrived at Zidadi.

367
18:43.780 --> 18:46.480
Legend has it he celebrated his newborn son's birth for three days

368
18:46.480 --> 18:47.720
and missed his chance to cross.

369
18:47.720 --> 18:50.250
Blocked by the river swollen from heavy rain,

370
18:50.430 --> 18:51.520
eventually,

371
18:52.190 --> 18:54.430
his army was annihilated by the Qing forces.

372
18:54.430 --> 18:56.400
The difficulties we're facing now

373
18:56.720 --> 18:59.810
are even greater than what he dealt with.

374
19:00.850 --> 19:01.490
Careful!

375
19:04.240 --> 19:05.670
Do you think 72 years ago,

376
19:05.980 --> 19:07.350
Shi Dakai's horses

377
19:07.480 --> 19:09.210
stepped on these exact stones?

378
19:09.890 --> 19:11.090
They definitely did,

379
19:14.460 --> 19:16.280
but certainly not this specific one.

380
19:16.280 --> 19:18.610
The Red Army will not repeat his mistakes.

381
19:18.810 --> 19:20.870
The path that proved a dead end for him

382
19:21.630 --> 19:23.490
is one we will surely get through.

383
19:29.480 --> 19:30.160
Let's go.

384
19:32.250 --> 19:33.010
Enlai!

385
19:33.390 --> 19:35.020
Was there a landslide up ahead?

386
19:35.020 --> 19:35.960
Are you guys okay?

387
19:35.960 --> 19:37.360
We're fine. Don't worry!

388
19:37.520 --> 19:38.800
Everyone, stay safe!

389
19:41.420 --> 19:43.020
Watch out for falling rocks!

390
19:59.810 --> 20:00.810
Stay safe!

391
20:02.510 --> 20:04.640
Protect the torches, hurry!

392
20:06.890 --> 20:08.160
Stay safe!

393
20:12.700 --> 20:14.300
Be careful. Stay safe!

394
20:14.820 --> 20:15.460
Watch out!

395
20:15.620 --> 20:16.620
Sun Jixian!

396
20:17.170 --> 20:18.220
Sun Jixian!

397
20:18.400 --> 20:19.250
Here!

398
20:19.280 --> 20:20.550
How much farther to Anshunchang?

399
20:20.550 --> 20:22.660
[Sun Jixian, Commander of the 1st Battalion, 1st Red Regiment]

400
20:20.790 --> 20:21.790
Commander,

401
20:21.990 --> 20:23.790
it's only about half a mile away!

402
20:24.370 --> 20:25.400
Pick up the pace!

403
20:25.570 --> 20:27.420
We must take the ferry crossing before dawn.

404
20:27.420 --> 20:28.420
Yes, sir!

405
20:29.130 --> 20:30.460
Hurry! Pick up the pace!

406
20:30.570 --> 20:33.370
We have to cross this mountain before dawn. Hurry!

407
21:06.780 --> 21:08.780
How did your battles go?

408
21:09.010 --> 21:10.410
Captured any artillery?

409
21:11.000 --> 21:12.850
I got two mortars

410
21:12.880 --> 21:13.720
and two mountain guns.

411
21:13.720 --> 21:14.890
Well, then I've got

412
21:15.110 --> 21:15.920
three mortars

413
21:15.920 --> 21:16.810
and one mountain gun.

414
21:16.810 --> 21:18.230
You guys are just bragging.

415
21:18.230 --> 21:19.710
I can tell you didn't...

416
21:20.930 --> 21:22.160
The Chairman is resting.

417
21:22.160 --> 21:23.920
The light went dim. Keep it down.

418
21:23.920 --> 21:25.720
Falsifying battle reports.

419
21:25.830 --> 21:26.710
Look at mine.

420
21:26.770 --> 21:27.830
Help me take a look.

421
21:29.330 --> 21:30.090
Look at mine.

422
21:30.120 --> 21:31.450
Is the Chairman inside?

423
21:32.600 --> 21:33.700
I have something to report to him.

424
21:33.700 --> 21:35.430
The Chairman just fell asleep.

425
21:35.540 --> 21:36.060
Come on.

426
21:36.090 --> 21:37.220
He finally got to rest.

427
21:37.220 --> 21:39.280
Whatever it is, talk to him tomorrow.

428
21:42.270 --> 21:43.640
This is urgent.

429
21:44.280 --> 21:46.880
Didn't the Chairman ask me to visit the locals?

430
21:46.920 --> 21:47.850
I found someone.

431
21:47.970 --> 21:48.930
In the neighboring village,

432
21:48.930 --> 21:50.250
there's an old scholar from the Qing Dynasty

433
21:50.250 --> 21:51.220
named Song Dashun.

434
21:51.220 --> 21:52.220
He's 90 years old.

435
21:52.490 --> 21:53.180
They say he

436
21:53.240 --> 21:55.520
was in Shi Dakai's Taiping Army

437
21:55.370 --> 21:58.190
[Li Fuchun, Acting Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

438
21:55.550 --> 21:57.310
when they lost the battle at Zidadi.

439
21:57.310 --> 21:58.310
I was thinking,

440
21:58.550 --> 22:00.260
could this help us cross the river?

441
22:00.260 --> 22:02.350
So I rushed over to report to the Chairman.

442
22:02.350 --> 22:03.310
No, I have to tell him.

443
22:03.310 --> 22:04.240
The Chairman...

444
22:05.630 --> 22:06.560
Comrade Fuchun,

445
22:08.390 --> 22:09.910
let's head over there right now.

446
22:09.910 --> 22:10.700
Chairman,

447
22:10.910 --> 22:12.170
you marched all day to the base,

448
22:12.170 --> 22:13.400
and started working right away.

449
22:13.400 --> 22:14.430
You're pushing yourself too hard.

450
22:14.430 --> 22:15.520
How about this?

451
22:15.580 --> 22:17.040
I'll invite him over here.

452
22:17.220 --> 22:18.870
We're seeking his advice.

453
22:18.940 --> 22:21.390
It makes no sense to ask the old man to come to us.

454
22:21.390 --> 22:22.110
Let's go.

455
22:22.710 --> 22:23.470
Alright.

456
22:25.130 --> 22:29.960
[Outskirts of Anshunchang Ferry, Sichuan]

457
22:43.810 --> 22:44.640
Sun Jixian,

458
22:48.390 --> 22:49.320
remember,

459
22:49.700 --> 22:51.040
after the 1st Battalion takes the ferry crossing,

460
22:51.040 --> 22:52.240
light a fire immediately to send a signal.

461
22:52.240 --> 22:53.640
Then look for boats and boatmen.

462
22:53.640 --> 22:54.430
Understood?

463
22:54.500 --> 22:55.370
Understood.

464
22:55.540 --> 22:57.000
Rest assured, Commander.

465
22:57.920 --> 22:58.680
Let's go!

466
23:26.360 --> 23:27.360
Comrade Bocheng!

467
23:28.590 --> 23:29.590
Comrade Bocheng!

468
23:30.510 --> 23:31.110
Rongzhen.

469
23:32.590 --> 23:33.500
Lie down, quickly.

470
23:33.500 --> 23:34.670
I'm fine. Go ahead.

471
23:34.910 --> 23:35.710
What is it?

472
23:36.170 --> 23:37.780
Yang Dezhi sent someone to report.

473
23:37.780 --> 23:38.770
The vanguard 1st Battalion

474
23:38.770 --> 23:41.830
has successfully occupied the Anshunchang Ferry crossing.

475
23:41.830 --> 23:43.020
Have they found any boats?

476
23:43.020 --> 23:43.790
The enemy had already

477
23:43.790 --> 23:45.710
burned the boats near the crossing.

478
23:45.710 --> 23:48.040
They're searching everywhere right now.

479
23:49.120 --> 23:52.920
How much farther to Anshunchang?

480
23:53.020 --> 23:54.060
Not far.

481
23:54.510 --> 23:55.910
Once we cross the mountain ahead,

482
23:55.910 --> 23:57.360
we'll be able to see Anshunchang.

483
23:57.360 --> 23:58.250
Good.

484
23:58.630 --> 24:00.230
We need to get there quickly.

485
24:01.020 --> 24:02.570
Send someone to tell Yang Dezhi

486
24:02.570 --> 24:03.370
to find boats.

487
24:03.450 --> 24:03.890
Okay.

488
24:03.920 --> 24:05.160
We must find boats.

489
24:05.900 --> 24:07.180
Once they find them,

490
24:07.370 --> 24:08.900
send a signal immediately.

491
24:09.360 --> 24:09.970
Rest assured.

492
24:09.970 --> 24:11.170
Move!

493
24:11.330 --> 24:13.730
Lie back down. Your health is what matters.

494
24:13.780 --> 24:14.980
Take good care of him.

495
24:16.450 --> 24:17.630
Hurry up in the front!

496
24:17.630 --> 24:18.830
Keep up in the back!

497
24:36.160 --> 24:36.890
Changbao.

498
24:38.920 --> 24:39.780
Did I scare you?

499
24:39.920 --> 24:41.050
Vice Chairman Zhou.

500
24:41.730 --> 24:43.560
Has Comrade Zedong rested?

501
24:44.010 --> 24:44.940
He and Deputy Director Li

502
24:44.940 --> 24:47.010
went to find a ninety-year-old scholar.

503
24:47.010 --> 24:48.340
If it's an emergency,

504
24:48.450 --> 24:49.520
I'll go find the Chairman right now.

505
24:49.520 --> 24:50.210
No need.

506
24:51.420 --> 24:52.680
I'll wait for him here.

507
24:53.240 --> 24:54.450
-Then I'll wait with you. -No need.

508
24:54.450 --> 24:55.510
Go get some rest.

509
24:56.030 --> 24:57.370
Jinbiao, have some rest.

510
24:57.370 --> 24:58.500
Vice Chairman Zhou.

511
24:58.870 --> 24:59.630
Just go.

512
24:59.530 --> 25:01.770
[Fan Jinbiao, Zhou Enlai's Guard]

513
24:59.710 --> 25:00.470
Yes, sir.

514
25:02.150 --> 25:02.910
Changbao,

515
25:03.170 --> 25:04.820
get me a map.

516
25:05.110 --> 25:05.830
Yes, sir.

517
25:23.790 --> 25:24.310
Okay.

518
25:25.050 --> 25:26.000
Go back and rest.

519
25:28.040 --> 25:29.310
[Hu Changbao, Squad Leader of Mao Zedong's Guard Squad]

520
25:29.770 --> 25:30.770
That's an order.

521
25:31.550 --> 25:32.200
Yes, sir.

522
26:32.480 --> 26:33.610
You guys go to sleep.

523
26:34.170 --> 26:35.650
Go to sleep. Get some rest.

524
26:36.200 --> 26:37.530
Go get some sleep.

525
27:36.070 --> 27:37.070
You're back?

526
27:37.990 --> 27:38.730
Enlai,

527
27:40.570 --> 27:41.770
I saw you were asleep.

528
27:42.080 --> 27:44.540
Since you're up, get back and have some rest.

529
27:44.710 --> 27:45.560
I'm fine.

530
27:45.850 --> 27:47.580
What did the old gentleman say?

531
27:50.910 --> 27:53.840
The old man told me

532
27:53.860 --> 27:55.790
the reason for Shi Dakai's defeat.

533
27:56.590 --> 27:57.960
He lacked the right timing,

534
27:57.960 --> 27:59.620
the geographical advantage,

535
27:59.700 --> 28:01.360
and the support of the people.

536
28:06.150 --> 28:07.110
I told him

537
28:07.620 --> 28:10.290
our Red Army isn't Shi Dakai.

538
28:16.660 --> 28:17.940
Go get some rest.

539
28:18.340 --> 28:20.000
I'll think about it some more.

540
28:21.380 --> 28:23.020
I wouldn't be able to sleep even if I went back.

541
28:23.020 --> 28:24.080
I'll stay with you.

542
28:56.090 --> 29:00.750
[Anshunchang Ferry, Dadu River, Sichuan]

543
29:12.190 --> 29:14.940
[Yang Dezhi, Commander of the 1st Regiment, 1st Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

544
29:14.530 --> 29:15.170
Check over there.

545
29:15.170 --> 29:15.700
Yes, sir.

546
29:34.020 --> 29:35.740
Who's in there? Come out!

547
29:38.740 --> 29:39.900
Spare us, officer!

548
29:42.640 --> 29:43.640
Stop right there!

549
29:44.310 --> 29:46.400
Officer, we're just civilians.

550
29:48.030 --> 29:49.000
Civilians?

551
29:49.640 --> 29:50.870
What are you doing here?

552
29:50.870 --> 29:51.800
We...

553
29:52.270 --> 29:53.090
We...

554
29:53.160 --> 29:53.850
Speak!

555
29:54.490 --> 29:55.160
Officer,

556
29:55.310 --> 29:57.670
I'm a servant for the wealthy Lai family in town.

557
29:57.670 --> 29:59.490
Our young master is a Nationalist battalion commander.

558
29:59.490 --> 30:01.280
He left a boat here,

559
30:01.640 --> 30:03.530
and we're watching it for him.

560
30:03.730 --> 30:04.730
Where's the boat?

561
30:04.980 --> 30:07.040
Hidden in the small woods over there.

562
30:07.100 --> 30:07.810
How many boats?

563
30:07.810 --> 30:08.640
Just one.

564
30:09.120 --> 30:09.980
Tell the truth!

565
30:10.250 --> 30:11.640
It really is just one.

566
30:12.530 --> 30:13.090
Li!

567
30:13.110 --> 30:13.620
Here!

568
30:13.650 --> 30:14.930
Tell the 1st Battalion to tow the boat.

569
30:14.930 --> 30:15.610
Yes, sir.

570
30:27.920 --> 30:28.450
Hurry up!

571
30:28.480 --> 30:29.400
Easy.

572
30:29.590 --> 30:30.320
Take it easy.

573
30:31.790 --> 30:32.920
Watch your step.

574
30:33.190 --> 30:34.360
Watch your step.

575
30:35.120 --> 30:36.270
Watch your step.

576
30:36.590 --> 30:37.120
Get back!

577
30:37.410 --> 30:39.070
Keep looking for other boats.

578
30:39.650 --> 30:41.490
Easy, don't bump it.

579
30:44.480 --> 30:45.200
Push!

580
30:45.510 --> 30:46.750
One, two!

581
30:46.980 --> 30:48.110
Careful.

582
30:48.450 --> 30:49.170
Hurry!

583
30:52.400 --> 30:53.640
Sun Jixian!

584
31:06.650 --> 31:07.740
Reporting to the Chief of Staff!

585
31:07.740 --> 31:09.590
Sun Jixian, damn you!

586
31:09.650 --> 31:11.160
Why didn't you send the signal?

587
31:11.160 --> 31:11.610
I...

588
31:12.630 --> 31:13.540
Reporting to the commander,

589
31:13.540 --> 31:13.900
I...

590
31:13.970 --> 31:15.310
I forgot to light the fire.

591
31:15.310 --> 31:17.780
Chief of Staff, I take full responsibility for this.

592
31:17.780 --> 31:20.910
Everyone was just focused on finding boats and boatmen.

593
31:24.890 --> 31:26.480
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps and the Central Red Army's Advance Detachment]

594
31:31.430 --> 31:33.220
It's rare to hear the Chief of Staff swear.

595
31:33.220 --> 31:35.510
You guys really got him worried.

596
31:38.910 --> 31:40.040
Sir,

597
31:40.400 --> 31:41.130
sir,

598
31:41.760 --> 31:44.350
how many people can this boat hold?

599
31:45.400 --> 31:47.010
Including us boatmen,

600
31:47.160 --> 31:49.290
it can take over a dozen people at once.

601
32:00.950 --> 32:01.710
Sun Jixian!

602
32:02.890 --> 32:03.530
Here!

603
32:03.720 --> 32:06.100
I was too hasty just now.

604
32:06.910 --> 32:08.110
I apologize.

605
32:08.470 --> 32:09.960
Your battalion, rest immediately.

606
32:09.960 --> 32:11.720
Later, I'll buy all the best food in town

607
32:11.720 --> 32:12.770
for you guys.

608
32:13.260 --> 32:15.230
Eat first, then start crossing the river.

609
32:15.230 --> 32:15.860
Yes, sir.

610
33:24.610 --> 33:25.570
Comrade Fuchun.

611
33:25.840 --> 33:26.800
What is it?

612
33:27.550 --> 33:29.280
Chairman, Vice Chairman Zhou.

613
33:29.550 --> 33:31.010
Telegram from Liu and Nie.

614
33:31.600 --> 33:33.330
They have occupied the Anshunchang Ferry.

615
33:33.330 --> 33:35.490
And they found a boat.

616
33:36.830 --> 33:37.940
Only one boat?

617
33:38.230 --> 33:39.360
Only one that works.

618
33:39.470 --> 33:41.730
And it can only hold about a dozen people.

619
33:42.340 --> 33:43.400
Xue Yue's Central Army

620
33:43.400 --> 33:44.550
has already approached Lizhou

621
33:44.550 --> 33:47.010
and will soon advance towards Anshunchang.

622
33:47.480 --> 33:49.500
Also, on the north bank of the Dadu River,

623
33:49.500 --> 33:50.700
Yang Sen's 20th Army

624
33:50.840 --> 33:52.690
is pushing towards Jinkouhe.

625
33:53.190 --> 33:56.120
They are less than three days away from Anshunchang.

626
34:08.170 --> 34:09.500
We can't stay here long.

627
34:10.489 --> 34:11.489
Besides here,

628
34:11.600 --> 34:13.460
where else can we cross the river?

629
34:16.530 --> 34:17.389
Luding Bridge.

630
34:53.110 --> 34:53.980
Attention!

631
34:54.969 --> 34:55.550
At ease.

632
34:57.000 --> 34:57.930
Xiong Shanglin!

633
34:57.950 --> 34:58.550
Here!

634
34:58.720 --> 34:59.510
Luo Huiming!

635
34:59.680 --> 35:00.360
Here!

636
35:00.610 --> 35:01.490
Liu Changfa!

637
35:01.650 --> 35:02.370
Here!

638
35:02.690 --> 35:03.560
Zhang Biaoke!

639
35:03.880 --> 35:04.590
Here!

640
35:04.800 --> 35:05.670
Zhang Guicheng!

641
35:05.670 --> 35:06.320
Here!

642
35:06.360 --> 35:07.320
Xiao Hanyao!

643
35:07.440 --> 35:08.190
Here!

644
35:08.230 --> 35:09.070
Wang Huating!

645
35:09.150 --> 35:09.670
Here!

646
35:09.880 --> 35:10.710
Liao Hongshan!

647
35:10.710 --> 35:11.230
Here!

648
35:11.510 --> 35:12.320
Lai Qiufa!

649
35:12.400 --> 35:12.960
Here!

650
35:13.170 --> 35:14.000
Zeng Xianji!

651
35:14.080 --> 35:14.770
Here!

652
35:14.790 --> 35:15.520
Guo Shicang!

653
35:15.670 --> 35:16.230
Here!

654
35:16.510 --> 35:17.440
Zhang Chengqiu!

655
35:17.600 --> 35:18.210
Here!

656
35:18.590 --> 35:19.420
Xiao Guilan!

657
35:19.540 --> 35:20.190
Here!

658
35:20.550 --> 35:21.300
Zhu Xiangyun!

659
35:21.300 --> 35:21.940
Here!

660
35:21.970 --> 35:22.830
Xie Liangming!

661
35:23.000 --> 35:23.670
Here!

662
35:23.920 --> 35:24.760
Ding Liumin!

663
35:24.780 --> 35:25.410
Here!

664
35:25.590 --> 35:26.310
Chen Wanqing!

665
35:26.310 --> 35:26.940
Here!

666
35:27.670 --> 35:29.200
Chief of Staff, reporting!

667
35:31.260 --> 35:33.390
Assembly complete, awaiting orders!

668
35:53.610 --> 35:54.480
Comrades!

669
35:54.390 --> 35:55.870
[Zhao Zhangcheng, Commander of the Artillery Company, 1st Red Army Corps]

670
35:54.830 --> 35:57.710
Do you remember the slogan we shouted

671
35:58.630 --> 36:00.360
during the Xiang River Battle?

672
36:00.440 --> 36:01.920
Fight to the death to survive!

673
36:01.920 --> 36:03.250
Fight to the death to survive!

674
36:03.250 --> 36:04.710
Fight to the death to survive!

675
36:04.710 --> 36:07.170
That's right. Fight to the death to survive!

676
36:07.850 --> 36:09.120
Now our Red Army

677
36:09.290 --> 36:11.430
once again faces a fight for survival.

678
36:12.260 --> 36:13.410
Ahead of us,

679
36:13.650 --> 36:16.400
the turbulent Dadu River blocks our way.

680
36:16.770 --> 36:18.170
Behind us are the CPC Central Committee

681
36:18.170 --> 36:21.330
and tens of thousands of our Red Army comrades.

682
36:21.870 --> 36:23.180
Hundreds of thousands of vicious enemies

683
36:23.180 --> 36:26.390
surround us.

684
36:26.960 --> 36:28.360
We have no way to retreat.

685
36:29.940 --> 36:32.630
We don't even have a moment to catch our breath.

686
36:33.440 --> 36:35.040
We must keep moving forward,

687
36:35.500 --> 36:36.890
no matter what.

688
36:37.630 --> 36:39.390
March towards the opposite bank!

689
36:39.390 --> 36:40.800
March towards the enemy!

690
36:41.380 --> 36:43.030
March towards death!

691
36:43.880 --> 36:45.540
March towards final victory!

692
36:46.480 --> 36:47.510
Advance!

693
36:47.530 --> 36:48.410
Yes, sir!

694
36:48.650 --> 36:49.690
Move out!

695
37:04.770 --> 37:06.040
At this very moment,

696
37:06.220 --> 37:08.080
in faraway Shanghai, a film about

697
37:08.510 --> 37:11.390
resisting Japanese aggression,

698
37:11.410 --> 37:13.670
Children of Troubled Times, is playing.

699
37:14.210 --> 37:16.040
The film's theme song,

700
37:16.070 --> 37:18.600
with lyrics by Tian Han and music by Nie Er,

701
37:18.830 --> 37:21.750
was named "March of the Volunteers".

702
37:22.410 --> 37:24.780
Fourteen years later, in 1949,

703
37:25.170 --> 37:26.040
this song

704
37:26.070 --> 37:30.270
became the provisional national anthem of the People's Republic of China.

705
37:38.740 --> 37:39.620
Attack!

706
39:55.850 --> 39:56.850
Zhao Zhangcheng!

707
39:56.990 --> 39:57.570
Here!

708
39:57.670 --> 39:58.770
Destroy the enemy's bunkers.

709
39:58.770 --> 39:59.690
Yes, sir.

710
41:13.130 --> 41:18.140
[Temporary Headquarters of the Military Commission, the Anshunchang Ferry, Sichuan]

711
41:20.230 --> 41:20.860
Comrade Bocheng.

712
41:20.860 --> 41:21.630
-Commanders. -Commanders.

713
41:21.630 --> 41:22.690
Comrade Rongzhen,

714
41:22.810 --> 41:23.890
you've been through a lot

715
41:23.890 --> 41:25.080
to cross the Dadu River.

716
41:25.080 --> 41:25.890
Not at all.

717
41:26.290 --> 41:27.870
What's the current situation with the river crossing?

718
41:27.870 --> 41:29.930
We've encountered a tricky problem.

719
41:30.040 --> 41:31.200
There are a limited number of boats.

720
41:31.200 --> 41:32.730
Besides, on the Dadu River,

721
41:32.850 --> 41:34.410
it is simply impossible to build a bridge.

722
41:34.410 --> 41:35.840
We tried to build a bridge several times,

723
41:35.840 --> 41:36.840
but failed every time.

724
41:36.840 --> 41:38.360
The wooden boats can only carry a limited number of people.

725
41:38.360 --> 41:39.150
So far,

726
41:39.180 --> 41:40.880
only the 1st Regiment has crossed the river.

727
41:40.880 --> 41:41.920
I've calculated it.

728
41:41.920 --> 41:42.840
At this rate,

729
41:43.070 --> 41:44.400
for the main force to cross the river completely,

730
41:44.400 --> 41:46.250
it will take at least twenty days.

731
41:46.250 --> 41:47.810
However, according to the current situation,

732
41:47.810 --> 41:49.070
the enemy's main force

733
41:49.070 --> 41:50.510
will take as little as three days

734
41:50.510 --> 41:51.840
to reach Anshunchang.

735
41:51.860 --> 41:52.530
Yes.

736
41:52.660 --> 41:53.200
Regarding this point,

737
41:53.200 --> 41:54.880
Comrade Bocheng and I have also considered it.

738
41:54.880 --> 41:56.220
During the 1st Regiment's river crossing,

739
41:56.220 --> 41:58.720
enemy reconnaissance planes flew over our heads twice.

740
41:58.720 --> 42:00.600
Chiang Kai-shek will also know about this situation.

741
42:00.600 --> 42:03.930
I'm afraid their pursuing forces will close in even faster.

742
42:05.330 --> 42:06.330
Luding Bridge.

743
42:08.310 --> 42:09.440
Take Luding Bridge.

744
42:10.520 --> 42:11.780
If one road is blocked,

745
42:11.920 --> 42:13.180
then take another one.

746
42:15.490 --> 42:18.050
I did consider Luding Bridge,

747
42:18.670 --> 42:19.940
but there are two concerns.

748
42:19.940 --> 42:20.610
First,

749
42:20.840 --> 42:22.110
Luding Bridge is 320 li

750
42:22.110 --> 42:23.280
from Anshunchang.

751
42:23.440 --> 42:24.400
Going upstream along the river,

752
42:24.400 --> 42:26.050
it's all rugged uphill mountain roads,

753
42:26.050 --> 42:28.110
and guarded by enemies along the way.

754
42:28.440 --> 42:30.960
We don't have much confidence in arriving in a short time.

755
42:30.960 --> 42:31.510
Second,

756
42:31.770 --> 42:33.960
the current situation at Luding Bridge is unknown.

757
42:33.960 --> 42:35.280
There are indeed difficulties,

758
42:35.280 --> 42:36.410
but some difficulties

759
42:36.410 --> 42:38.140
are inevitable no matter what.

760
42:38.410 --> 42:39.670
Instead of hesitating

761
42:39.670 --> 42:40.840
and pacing back and forth,

762
42:40.840 --> 42:42.280
we might as well face the difficulties head-on.

763
42:42.280 --> 42:43.550
Defending Anshunchang to the death

764
42:43.550 --> 42:45.880
is exactly what Shi Dakai did 72 years ago.

765
42:46.200 --> 42:48.710
Our idea is to divide our forces into two routes,

766
42:48.710 --> 42:51.000
splitting into left and right columns to act simultaneously,

767
42:51.000 --> 42:53.400
to capture Luding Bridge and then reunite.

768
42:54.020 --> 42:57.470
Take the 1st Division and the Cadre Regiment as the right column.

769
42:57.470 --> 42:58.930
You two will take command,

770
42:59.630 --> 43:01.950
and after crossing the river at Anshunchang,

771
43:01.950 --> 43:03.830
push north along the east bank.
